<title>UK: Phillips says shuts 100,000 bpd UK Tees refinery.</title>
<headline>Phillips says shuts 100,000 bpd UK Tees refinery.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Phillips Petroleum Co  said on Friday its 100,000 barrels-per-day refinery on north Tees was shut for inspection after a small fire on Thursday.  </p>
<p>&quot;The refinery is off-line after a very small fire yesterday,&quot; spokeswoman Paula Hopson said. &quot;I don't know when it will be back up again, It could be today, it could be tomorrow. We'll have to wait and see.&quot;</p>
<p>The refinery, in northeast England, is jointly owned by Phillips and Imperial Chemical Industries Plc (ICI).</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7714</p>
